---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base title="Coverage and Site Confirmation | HeyDock" description="HeyDock confirms each UK site before a visit is booked. We do not publish a coverage map that pretends every postcode is guaranteed." canonicalPath="/coverage" keywords="IT engineer coverage UK, on-site IT availability, HeyDock coverage">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Coverage</p>
    <h1>We confirm the site, we do not assume the map</h1>
    <p class="lede">Tell us the town, the task and the window. We will say whether we can attend, rather than implying a national guarantee.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section white"><div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>How confirmation works</h2>
    <p>On-site work is booked only when the city, the skills, the access and the window can be confirmed. Some locations will not be possible on the timescale you want. European or unusual sites are treated the same way: confirmed per request, including language and scheduling constraints.</p>
    <p>Remote work can often start sooner, if the systems can be reached safely. A coverage question can also be sent through the <a href="/contact?service=coverage">enquiry form</a> with 'Coverage / location check' selected.</p>
    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <p>We will not publish a heat map that over-promises. We will not treat a same-day visit as a default. We will not quietly send someone under-skilled to 'make a start'.</p>
  </div></section>
  <CtaBand service="coverage" title="Check a location" />
</Base>
